      {
        "value": "threatened",
        "source": "elcat-v2024.1",
        "note": "still learnt consistently by almost all children as either the first language (in monolingual families) or as the community language (in families bilingual in Khamnigan Mongol and Khamnigan Evenki); although vigorous for the moment, the survival of Khamnigan Mongol in the long run is threatened by the increasing influx of Han Chinese settlers; both Chinese and Standard Mongolian are also present via the networks of radio and television as well as in the form of printed material [Endangerment.Certainty: 0.8]",
        "scale": "elcat-v2024.1"
      },
